GLM-5.3-Flash two-Spark engine (patches/0001-spark-stack-060.patch, src/tensorfold/families/glm5_next/spark/)
  TensorFold 0.3.4's GLM CUDA engine (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TensorFold contributors) with the
  glm53-tensorfold-spark patch series (https://github.com/jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark, MIT for the engine
  changes, Copyright (c) 2026 Jay Leaton), rebased onto TensorFold 0.6.0. It contains code adapted from:

  b12x "RoCEnante" RoCE collectives and fast-prefill kernels
    local-inference-lab/b12x (https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x), Copyright 2026 Luke Alonso and the
    b12x contributors, Apache License 2.0 (b12x ships no NOTICE file). roce.cpp, roce.cu, roce_common.h and
    roce.py adapt its RDMA proxy, all-gather kernel, PTX intrinsics and one-shot protocol (b12x/comm/roce/);
    b12x_kda.py, b12x_mhc.py and b12x_attn.py re-implement algorithms of b12x's kda_prefill, norm.mhc and
    attention.sparse_mla in Triton without copying code. The changes are listed in the files' headers.

  GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark serving kits
    Reederey87/glm53-flash-exl3-2x-dgx-spark (commit 6c337d2), Apache License 2.0, itself based on the kit by
    Mia's AI Lab (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks), MIT License for the
    contributions made before 2026-09-07 (Copyright (c) 2026 Mia's AI Lab; that repository is AGPL-3.0 since
    then). The "fat" expert kernels in exl3_fast.cu (namespace fat) adapt the structure of that kit's grouped
    fat-expert MoE (cp.async-staged trellis tiles, gate/up sharing one rotated input, XOR-swizzled stages, the
    ticket scheduler); the arithmetic is the engine's own. The KDA bf16 projection copy re-implements the idea of
    MiaAI-Lab PR #233 (AGPL-3.0) without its code. Reederey87's NOTICE is reproduced at the end of this file.

  kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 (ideas only)
    The repository has no licence; exl3_fat2.cu re-implements the structure of its fused prefill MoE kernel on
    the engine's arithmetic, and NCCL over both CX7 functions follows its notes. No code is included.

  log / exp of ARM Optimized Routines as built into glibc 2.39
    gpusample.py re-implements for the GPU the float64 log and exp numpy calls on aarch64 (glibc 2.39's __log /
    __exp, from https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines; Copyright (c) Arm Limited; MIT OR Apache-2.0
    WITH LLVM-exception), with their coefficient and lookup tables, so the GPU sampler's bits equal the host's.

  Later upstream TensorFold releases (0.3.6.2, 0.5.0)
    server/cancellation.py, image_fetch.py, grammar.py's closed_json / parse_numbers and the /health totals port
    MIT code of those releases (Copyright (c) 2026 TensorFold contributors); each ported piece names its source
    commit.

  Public text behind the shipped GLM draft-vocabulary ranking (draft_vocab.txt)
    Token ids ordered by frequency, counted by the GLM recipe's bench/draftvocab_public.py in OpenAssistant/oasst1
    (Apache-2.0), SWE-Gym/OpenHands-SFT-Trajectories (MIT), CPython 3.14.7 Lib/ and Doc/ (PSF License 2.0),
    denoland/std (MIT) and BurntSushi/ripgrep 14.1.1 (MIT OR Unlicense). No text of these sources is included.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (patches/0002)
  tests/fixtures/dsv41_encoding_ref.py is DeepSeek's encoding/encoding.py of deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, copied
  unchanged as test data (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek). The family's math follows vLLM's DeepSeek-V4 /
  V4.1 model code (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, Apache License 2.0), cited in each module; no code is
  copied. The EXL3 pack layout and the packed Engram shard format are read from the files (file-format facts);
  nothing is taken from the MiaAI-Lab DeepSeek kit's AGPL-3.0 overlay or chat template.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash encoding reference (tests/serving/data/encoding_dsv41_ref.py)
  DeepSeek's encoding/encoding.py of deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, copied unchanged as test data (MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek). The development reference model in engine/reference/ follows vLLM's and DeepSeek's
  reference math (cited per module); no code is copied.

MiaAI-Lab DeepSeek-V4.1 kit output (results/campaign/, results/kit-baseline/)
  Logs, metrics and benchmark output of the kit (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks)
  as measured on our pair, including its effective configuration; no kit code.

MMLU (bench/data/mmlu200.jsonl)
  200 questions of the MMLU test set (Hendrycks et al., https://github.com/hendrycks/test), MIT License.

xgrammar (structured output)
  mlc-ai/xgrammar 0.2.8 (https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar), Apache License 2.0, installed into the image by
  docker/Dockerfile with pip, with transformers (Apache-2.0); not vendored.

NVIDIA PyTorch container (nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.07-py3)
  The Docker image is built FROM this container and is subject to the NVIDIA Deep Learning Container License.
  PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause) and Triton (MIT) come from it.

Not included; each user downloads these under their own terms:

  DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash): the original checkpoint, used for the Engram tables
